      <h3>The Marker Method</h3>
      <p>For any tool whose geometry is not on the setter &mdash; the roughing gouge, parting tool and scrapers in this kit, or a gouge you want to keep at a non-chart grind &mdash; black the bevel with a felt marker, put the tool in its jig on the support, and turn the wheel backwards by hand. Move the support in or out until the stone wipes the ink off from the heel to the tip in one pass; then lock it. It is exact for any wheel diameter, just slower than dropping the setter over the bar. Write the JS and P you used on a label so only the support position needs to be rediscovered next time.</p>
