      <h2>Care and Storage</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything goes back in the TNT-00 tray inside the TC-800 case; the foam keeps the setter&rsquo;s contact discs and the jig seats from getting knocked about. The MH-380 cover goes over the T-8 between sessions.</li>
        <li>Dry the jigs after use; the SVS-50 and SVD-186 R are zinc and steel and will spot if put away wet. A wipe of light oil on the screws and the SVD-186 R sleeve keeps them sliding.</li>
        <li>Protect profile labels with a coat of clear varnish or a wrap of clear tape &mdash; they live under the water spray.</li>
        <li>The leather discs on the LA-120 want compound, not oil, after the first impregnation. If they glaze or go dark and hard, a light scrape and fresh PA-70 brings them back.</li>
        <li>Keep the stone graded and trued; a grooved or out-of-round stone defeats the setter, because the setter assumes the wheel surface is where the discs say it is.</li>
      </ul>
